From df31e9a3743c04214102709610d173ac670cdf79 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Ian Blenke <ian@blenke.com>
Date: Wed, 22 Jul 2026 20:06:35 -0400
Subject: [PATCH 07568/11362] [outer-loop] REQ-ARC-WMTE-5827: verifier-filtered
 reactive loop (no upfront symbolic induction)

Operator-directed architectural pivot, following the pre-registered
branch-2 decision in the 2026-07-20 induction-quality design doc: CEGIS
refinement of an induced symbolic world model does not lift a frozen
small model's induction quality (GAP-ARC-INDUCTION-REFINEMENT-NULL,
positive_game_frac=0.0 on two model sizes), corroborating "Falsification,
Not Exposure" (arXiv:2606.31511) -- frozen models can't self-correct from
feedback, only comparison against real ground truth reliably filters bad
outputs.

This module replaces explicit engine() synthesis with a per-step
propose-then-filter loop: the generator proposes one action, a real
verifier (exact-match dead-end rejection + the already-trained,
already live-validated FrameChangeScorer CNN) filters it before commit.
Preserves Carnot's verification-first thesis rather than adopting Duck
Harness's unverified reactive loop wholesale.

Two real bugs found and fixed while building this (not assumed):
arc_llm_guided_solve.py's own proposal loop calls proposer.generate(),
which is hardcoded for Python code synthesis (ast.parse regardless of
`validate`) -- it has likely never worked for a free-text JSON task.
And the obvious fix (raw completion, then chat-completions) both failed
to suppress this GGUF's reasoning; the fix that works reuses the
project's own proven fence-priming + stop-sequence pattern from the
induce task's _L2_CODEONLY_DIRECTIVE.

10 unit tests (pure filter logic, no GPU). A real 3-game empirical A/B
(scripts/arc_reactive_verifier_filter_ab.py) against exp5727's already-
measured induce-then-plan baseline is running separately; results will
land in a follow-up commit regardless of outcome.

